1
00:00:15,657 --> 00:00:17,118
Good evening.

2
00:00:17,138 --> 00:00:19,341
I trust you had a fruitful day.

3
00:00:19,361 --> 00:00:20,724
I did not say happy.

4
00:00:20,763 --> 00:00:22,265
I hope it has been happy.

5
00:00:22,306 --> 00:00:31,498
Namotasa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhodasa.

6
00:00:31,518 --> 00:00:39,149
Namotasa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhodasa.

7
00:00:40,024 --> 00:00:48,692
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambuddhasa.

8
00:00:48,713 --> 00:00:52,996
Homage to the Buddha, the blessed, noble and fully self-awakened one.

9
00:00:54,859 --> 00:00:57,960
Could you just tell me if the sound is okay?

10
00:01:00,624 --> 00:01:02,466
Can you put a little note in there for me?

11
00:01:07,049 --> 00:01:09,492
We've got a new laptop, you see.

12
00:01:09,876 --> 00:01:15,361
And I'm hoping it's using the sound from this little camera.

13
00:01:18,183 --> 00:01:19,905
Yeah, is the sound all right?

14
00:01:22,908 --> 00:01:24,728
Sounds fine, thank you very much.

15
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:28,132
Okay.

16
00:01:28,152 --> 00:01:30,694
So we're tackling this problem of karma.

17
00:01:34,376 --> 00:01:39,781
So just let me repeat the sort of basic phrase that the Buddha uses, the basic formula.

18
00:01:40,555 --> 00:01:43,477
Beings are owners of their actions, right?

19
00:01:43,498 --> 00:01:44,138
You own it.

20
00:01:44,959 --> 00:01:47,001
You are heir to your actions.

21
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:50,144
Whatever consequences there are, they'll be yours.

22
00:01:51,566 --> 00:01:53,688
They originate from their actions.

23
00:01:53,787 --> 00:01:57,331
In other words, you're born of your actions, moment after moment.

24
00:01:58,591 --> 00:01:59,552
You're bound to them.

25
00:01:59,813 --> 00:02:03,736
You're chained to your actions.

26
00:02:04,477 --> 00:02:07,760
And your actions are your refuge, hopefully a good refuge.

27
00:02:10,036 --> 00:02:14,640
It is action that distinguishes between inferior and superior.

28
00:02:14,661 --> 00:02:16,663
And then we went through various things.

29
00:02:16,703 --> 00:02:20,426
Now you have to remember these are very broad brushstrokes, right?

30
00:02:21,048 --> 00:02:36,465
I mean, if some man or woman, if, if we were to go around killing murderers, bloody handed, given to blows and violence, if we did that all our lives, then we will surely end up in a dreadful place, but we don't do that all our lives.

31
00:02:36,731 --> 00:02:37,673
It's a big mixture.

32
00:02:38,152 --> 00:02:46,681
We also like to abstain from such things and take care of animals and stuff like that, you see.

33
00:02:47,022 --> 00:02:52,768
So our lives are a balance between those things that are unskilful, those things that are skillful.

34
00:02:52,788 --> 00:03:04,139
So it becomes impossible to say what our destiny is, except in that broadest way that if we've been generally good, we should be okay.

35
00:03:06,263 --> 00:03:07,024
Breathe easy.

36
00:03:08,324 --> 00:03:22,257
Now, what I want to center on tonight is the fact that, of course, not everything that happens to us is our personal karma.

37
00:03:22,276 --> 00:03:23,337
So that's very important.

38
00:03:24,419 --> 00:03:35,628
So although the Buddha did not formalize this, these sections are taken from what he spoke at various times during

39
00:03:35,947 --> 00:03:41,894
his lifetime, and they're called niyama or laws.

40
00:03:43,294 --> 00:03:50,143
So the first one is to do with uttu, which is the season's energy.

41
00:03:50,502 --> 00:03:52,885
So it's to do with physics, chemistry, etc.

42
00:03:52,906 --> 00:03:55,609
It's to do with the mineral world.

43
00:03:57,411 --> 00:04:05,058
Now, as you know, for instance, we had a few years ago that terrible tsunami and killed

44
00:04:05,241 --> 00:04:34,572
many people so it would be foolish for those people to think well you know uh or foolish people to think that those people who ground must have done something terrible in their past lives when we're born on the earth um we are subject to the uh the physics of the earth the chemistry of the earth and as we and now when it comes to of course climate crisis that's something else because there we are we are definitely explicitly involved

45
00:04:35,026 --> 00:04:48,004
But when it comes to just natural disasters and we may be caught up in them, then it's just one of those things that we have to accept is part of the risk of becoming a human being.

46
00:04:51,428 --> 00:04:53,632
Now, the next one is Bija, which means seed.

47
00:04:53,651 --> 00:04:54,992
So that's all our genetics.

48
00:04:55,394 --> 00:05:04,846
So, again, it would be very wrong to think that somebody who was born with a hereditary disease somehow deserves it.

49
00:05:05,384 --> 00:05:18,521
That would be completely wrong because, well, we know that our genes are coming up from who knows where, and we've ended up with this particular combination.

50
00:05:18,541 --> 00:05:22,487
So there's not much to do with personal karma there.

51
00:05:23,668 --> 00:05:33,822
Although, of course, it's understood that the mind can have an effect on the body, but definitely I don't think it would be right to think of hereditary diseases or

52
00:05:34,105 --> 00:05:43,197
something that happens at birth through the birth process whereby the body is injured in some way as being personal karma.

53
00:05:43,918 --> 00:05:50,425
Now, what would be personal karma is, of course, how we relate to the body that we're in.

54
00:05:50,446 --> 00:05:54,050
Now, that comes elsewhere.

55
00:05:54,651 --> 00:06:03,403
But the actual body itself is what is given to us by our...

56
00:06:03,771 --> 00:06:04,653
our genes.

57
00:06:08,137 --> 00:06:11,841
Then there comes karma, of course, which we're actually going into.

58
00:06:12,302 --> 00:06:16,047
So that's the moral level of the universe.

59
00:06:16,086 --> 00:06:25,619
And that's really to do with how we feel inside ourselves, the meaningfulness of our lives, our happiness is very much tied in to our goodness.

60
00:06:28,141 --> 00:06:29,283
Although not necessarily.

61
00:06:29,302 --> 00:06:31,685
So of course, if you're if you're a sadist,

62
00:06:31,952 --> 00:06:34,935
then you might find some happiness in torturing people.

63
00:06:36,096 --> 00:06:38,819
So it's not always clear, clean cut.

64
00:06:39,321 --> 00:06:54,637
But what we can say is that whatever is not beneficial to us, not beneficial to others, or to both, will lead to an unhappy place, an unhappy place within us.

65
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,605
There are examples that come to mind.

66
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:08,920
If you remember the terrible Moores murders that went back in the 60s, Brady and Myra Hindley.

67
00:07:10,021 --> 00:07:15,410
So she seems to have come to some sort of forgiveness about it by being a Christian.

68
00:07:16,091 --> 00:07:24,062
But Brady went mad, of course, eventually, and seems to have been OK. You know, he got his mind back a bit.

69
00:07:24,081 --> 00:07:29,069
And when he was asked, did he ever think about the murders of those boys and girls?

70
00:07:29,911 --> 00:07:31,973
He says if he did, it would drive him mad.

71
00:07:32,093 --> 00:07:32,875
So there was

72
00:07:33,192 --> 00:07:37,216
it's obviously that something was boiling in him.

73
00:07:37,877 --> 00:07:51,553
And that, of course, would manifest in his later, in his rebirth, you know, if, well, he will be reborn, in Buddhist terms, and that will manifest.

74
00:07:51,574 --> 00:07:53,637
He'll have to work through that karma, you see.

75
00:07:54,958 --> 00:08:01,326
So it's the same even when you think of, you know, Stalin, Hitler, Pol Pot, all these people that we know have,

76
00:08:01,677 --> 00:08:12,750
perpetrated tremendous evils, they themselves will have to suffer the consequences of that.

77
00:08:12,771 --> 00:08:16,997
Then there's Dharma, the law of Dharma, the spiritual law.

78
00:08:17,057 --> 00:08:22,264
So this is, you know, the Four Noble Truths, basically, and everything that comes out of the Four Noble Truths.

79
00:08:22,983 --> 00:08:27,329
So that comes pretty straightforward.

80
00:08:27,670 --> 00:08:31,194
And, of course, involved in that is our karma, right?

81
00:08:31,579 --> 00:08:41,168
It's all to do with understanding how we create suffering, how we undermine that sense of suffering or unsatisfactoriness and liberate ourselves.

82
00:08:42,210 --> 00:08:44,192
And the final one is citta.

83
00:08:44,211 --> 00:08:45,413
So I've left that finally.

84
00:08:45,732 --> 00:08:47,815
Normally it doesn't come in the order that I've given.

85
00:08:47,855 --> 00:08:50,297
The citta is the heart mind.

86
00:08:52,479 --> 00:08:54,681
In the old days, you would have referred to it as the soul.

87
00:08:55,081 --> 00:08:56,482
The spirit was something else.

88
00:08:56,923 --> 00:09:00,826
So the closest word would be something like psyche.

89
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:04,495
both the heart and mind, emotional and thought life.

90
00:09:05,174 --> 00:09:08,719
And a lot of it is given, the way we perceive things.

91
00:09:10,059 --> 00:09:16,427
If you're born with poor hearing, then of course you won't hear so well.

92
00:09:16,826 --> 00:09:23,754
If you're born with color blindness, you'll see the world in a different way than other people see it.

93
00:09:24,274 --> 00:09:30,881
So the actual basis of contact with the world is also given to us, you see.

94
00:09:31,198 --> 00:09:41,912
And what we do with it inside, of course, is also to do very much with just our whole basic psychology.

95
00:09:42,692 --> 00:09:47,337
Behind, of course, then we have this relationship of wanting, not wanting.

96
00:09:48,119 --> 00:09:56,328
But I suppose with this terrible murder of George Floyd, the question

97
00:09:56,647 --> 00:10:01,773
of social karma comes into play.

98
00:10:02,394 --> 00:10:19,033
And anybody who sees that, I was trying not to see it, but my brother sent me the transcript of what he was pleading for, and I did actually go and watch it.

99
00:10:19,894 --> 00:10:22,118
Well, it's beyond words, isn't it?

100
00:10:23,239 --> 00:10:25,422
And what can we say?

101
00:10:26,025 --> 00:10:39,865
When we are born, we are born into a society and we are given, whether we like it or not, the ignorances, the delusions and the biases and the prejudices of that society.

102
00:10:41,067 --> 00:10:45,774
I'm a little bit confused the way people use bias and prejudice and all that.

103
00:10:46,134 --> 00:10:50,942
But in a sense, that prejudice remains within us as just a delusion.

104
00:10:51,121 --> 00:10:51,982
That's how we think.

105
00:10:52,672 --> 00:10:57,337
So every nation, every tribe thinks of itself as superior to others.

106
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:05,548
And that sense of superiority is just an extension of the self, an extension of the ego, of me.

107
00:11:06,048 --> 00:11:15,642
And of course, what the self does is it creates a fence, it creates a barrier, and it feels sort of safe

108
00:11:15,857 --> 00:11:18,600
when it has other people within the same corral.

109
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:24,547
So you've got lots of little egos, little selves all together supporting each other.

110
00:11:24,567 --> 00:11:30,273
And so the prejudices, the delusions of that society are maintained.

111
00:11:31,254 --> 00:11:40,543
And our job, our purpose is to really recognize a prejudice when it comes into our consciousness.

112
00:11:41,563 --> 00:11:45,628
And we may be slightly disturbed

113
00:11:45,845 --> 00:11:57,414
by how prejudicial we might be, just caught here and there in certain circumstances, racial prejudice, sexism and all that sort of stuff.

114
00:11:57,875 --> 00:12:05,422
And we have to be careful because we have this self-esteem which says, oh, you know, I'm not this, I'm not that.

115
00:12:06,022 --> 00:12:10,265
But when it comes up, you have to be quite honest to ourselves, right?

116
00:12:10,285 --> 00:12:15,210
It's impossible for people, for anybody in society not to be prejudiced.

117
00:12:15,645 --> 00:12:17,808
It's just part of our makeup.

118
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:32,087
Our purpose in terms of purifying our heart is to, first of all, really accept that everybody's prejudiced one way or the other in all these fields and to actually accept it.

119
00:12:32,548 --> 00:12:45,264
And then, of course, to recognize, to be sharp when it appears always first in the mind and to point to it and say, well, that's prejudiced, that's judgmental, you know, and not to indulge it.

120
00:12:45,986 --> 00:13:13,682
then very slowly uh it has less and less an effect as you know if something is is if something is repressed within us then it will manifest anyway i mean freudian slips and all that and um jung said something i thought was was a tremendous profundity he said whatever is repressed will manifest as fate will manifest as fate in other words

121
00:13:13,881 --> 00:13:31,960
whether you like it or not, all our suppressed feelings, all our repressed prejudices and feelings and all that are actually having an effect on the way we are moving now, affecting the way that we relate to people, the way that we're working, the way that we're in the world.

122
00:13:33,201 --> 00:13:43,871
They've done all sorts of studies during my time when I was a teacher about the way that teachers quite unconsciously

123
00:13:44,037 --> 00:14:03,943
treat girls and boys differently, how they treat people from ethnic groups, whether they are black people or whatever, Indians or whatever, coloured people, and white people, depending on whether the teacher themselves is white or otherwise.

124
00:14:04,565 --> 00:14:08,610
So all that's been heavily studied and quite well known.

125
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:19,434
And it's up to the teacher then to recognise those biases and not allow it to distort their teaching.

126
00:14:19,455 --> 00:14:32,033
So it's a really, really very difficult area for us to really be very truthful to ourselves about our own prejudices and to allow ourselves to be honest about it.

127
00:14:32,687 --> 00:14:36,614
And then to make that decision, well, you know, I'm not acting on it.

128
00:14:36,874 --> 00:14:41,041
So if we're not acting on it, there's no consequence.

129
00:14:41,061 --> 00:14:42,442
This is the law of karma.

130
00:14:43,323 --> 00:15:01,311
So whatever the desire is in this particular discussion about prejudice, whatever that desire is, so long as it remains as some idea, some intention in the mind, nothing's happened.

131
00:15:01,779 --> 00:15:04,003
I mean, that's really important to grasp.

132
00:15:04,023 --> 00:15:06,625
So there's no reason to feel guilt about it.

133
00:15:07,086 --> 00:15:09,168
There's no reason to feel shame about it.

134
00:15:09,669 --> 00:15:12,373
It's not necessary to do that.

135
00:15:12,393 --> 00:15:15,917
It's just necessary to say, oh, this is it.

136
00:15:16,038 --> 00:15:17,119
That's a racial thought.

137
00:15:17,198 --> 00:15:19,341
That's a sexist thought and so on.

138
00:15:19,361 --> 00:15:24,847
And to just stay above it, you know, just to stay with it and allow it to die away.

139
00:15:25,830 --> 00:15:29,374
And if we do get caught up in thoughts about it,

140
00:15:29,741 --> 00:15:45,965
to really, you know, pull ourselves off it and recognize it, sink into the heart, you know, and to be kind to ourselves, you see, and to be able to forgive ourselves, to be, you know, to actually say to ourselves, well, you know, that's part of my upbringing.

141
00:15:46,926 --> 00:15:51,893
That will always be there, you know, and this may come as a surprise.

142
00:15:52,052 --> 00:15:59,243
Those little conditionings will be there even if we are fully liberated.

143
00:15:59,695 --> 00:16:02,398
They're known as vasana.

144
00:16:02,418 --> 00:16:07,082
These vasanas are leftover traces of conditionings.

145
00:16:08,443 --> 00:16:14,429
But of course, in somebody who is liberated, it's impossible for them to be caught up in it.

146
00:16:17,072 --> 00:16:18,153
But they remain the mind.

147
00:16:18,313 --> 00:16:22,077
They will actually appear in given circumstances.

148
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:29,144
So recognizing that is

149
00:16:29,293 --> 00:16:56,414
basically our job to uh to be aware of any negativity especially prejudices and so on and so forth and and to just be honest about it you know and there's no there's no shame for that there's no there's no guilt that's just that's that's the part of the baggage that we end up being given when we're born into a society so uh this this is dreadful occasion which i hope

150
00:16:57,187 --> 00:17:06,421
I mean, people are saying that it may have a real fundamental change in America and across the world, hopefully.

151
00:17:08,625 --> 00:17:14,732
It's funny how something like that in plain sight can be truly shocking.

152
00:17:16,195 --> 00:17:23,465
I remember the Vietnam War, that picture, I'm sure you all remember it, the picture of that young girl

153
00:17:23,782 --> 00:17:33,517
Well, there were lots of them running, but there was that young girl, that naked young girl burning with napalm on her back from a bomb.

154
00:17:33,537 --> 00:17:43,611
And that sort of picture was just so shocking that I think it wasn't long after that that the Americans pulled out of Vietnam.

155
00:17:45,713 --> 00:17:53,065
So it's good to sit with these sorts of things and, you know, just bear with the

156
00:17:53,347 --> 00:18:21,364
the horror of it really so um well i can only hope my words have been of some assistance and that uh through our through all of our efforts to actually perceive what is unwholesome in us and not to activate it not to act upon it we will slowly liberate our hearts from all this negativity

157
00:18:22,828 --> 00:18:28,333
and become fully liberated from all suffering sooner rather than later.

